  "salt": "nKWiQ_CBOUgInO4gTV21Yg==",
  "text": "Salt is a symbolic material. The Celts drew much of their early wealth from it. Great mines worked near their center at Hallstatt in Austria. Inland peoples needed salt to keep meat through winter. They salted meat and fish. Salt was also traded for valuables from far away. On the continent the Celts used it as a plain commodity. Among the island Celts it gained a second meaning. Salt was thought to repel fairies. A traveler who carried salt was safe from their mischief. Even salted meat could shield a person on bad nights such as Samhain. Iron worked the same way, as nails and scissors. So salt became both a trade good and a charm.",
